The structure may evolve with implementation.


================================================================================
PROJECT ARTIFACTS
================================================================================

The project maintains four primary artifacts.


1. CURRENT STATE

    Exact state of the deployed environment.

    Contains:

        current phase
        current stage
        implemented components
        VM state
        networking state
        documentation state
        outstanding tasks


2. ROADMAP

    Overall project progression.

    Contains:

        phases
        stages
        progress
        current position
        completed work


3. CONSPECT

    Practical technical knowledge gathered during
    implementation.

    Contains:

        commands
        configurations
        concepts encountered
        troubleshooting conclusions
        important Q&A
        implementation notes


4. CONTEXT

    This document.

    Contains:

        project purpose
        architecture
        design principles
        roadmap
        implementation methodology
        TODO
        current-state model


Detailed implementation belongs in repository
documentation and procedures rather than this master context.


================================================================================
PROGRESS TRACKING
================================================================================

Progress is updated AFTER meaningful implementation milestones.


For each completed stage:


    IMPLEMENT
        ↓
    VERIFY
        ↓
    DOCUMENT
        ↓
    REVIEW
        ↓
    MARK COMPLETE
        ↓
    UPDATE PROJECT STATE
        ↓
    UPDATE PROGRESS


The roadmap should show:


    completed stages
    current stage
    remaining stages
    percentage


Do not mark a stage complete merely because
a tutorial or plan exists.


A stage is complete when its intended implementation
has been performed and verified.


================================================================================
DEFINITION OF DONE
================================================================================

The project is complete when the student can
independently operate and explain the resulting environment.


This includes:


    - manage the lab infrastructure
    - explain the network
    - add and manage VMs
    - administer Windows
    - administer Active Directory
    - manage users and groups
    - troubleshoot DNS and DHCP
    - manage permissions
    - support Windows endpoints
    - investigate incidents
    - manage ITSM workflows
    - manage assets and software
    - understand cloud IAM
    - deploy cloud resources in Floci
    - operate S3 / SQS / Lambda / RDS where supported
    - manage secrets
    - use Terraform
    - automate repetitive administration
    - use GitHub Actions
    - monitor infrastructure
    - troubleshoot failures
    - apply security principles
    - document infrastructure
    - explain architectural decisions


Most importantly:


    WHAT exists
        +
    WHY it exists
        +
    HOW it was implemented
        +
    HOW it is administered
        +
    HOW it is troubleshot
        +
    HOW the components interact


================================================================================
FINAL PROJECT STORY
================================================================================

The final portfolio story should be:


    "I designed, built and administered a small
     engineering company's internal IT environment,
     together with a local AWS-style cloud laboratory."


The implementation story:


    Lab Foundation
        ↓
    Networking
        ↓
    Cloud
        ↓
    Windows / Active Directory
        ↓
    IT Operations
        ↓
    Automation / IaC
        ↓
    ITSM
        ↓
    Monitoring
        ↓
    Final Integration


Cross-cutting throughout:


    Security
    Troubleshooting
    Documentation


Automation and IaC may also be introduced
incrementally before their dedicated phase
when implementation makes them useful.


================================================================================
CURRENT OPERATING MODEL
================================================================================

From this point forward, work should proceed as:


    CURRENT STATE
        ↓
    CURRENT STAGE
        ↓
    WHAT ARE WE BUILDING?
        ↓
    WHY DOES IT EXIST?
        ↓
    IMPLEMENT
        ↓
    VERIFY
        ↓
    TROUBLESHOOT IF NECESSARY
        ↓
    DOCUMENT / CONSPECT
        ↓
    REVIEW
        ↓
    UPDATE CURRENT STATE
        ↓
    UPDATE ROADMAP
        ↓
    NEXT STAGE


No standalone lectures unless the student
specifically asks for one.


If a concept is unclear:


    STOP briefly
        ↓
    explain the specific concept
        ↓
    connect it to the current implementation
        ↓
    continue building


The project always remains the primary activity.


